content.text:
The product page was blocking on `getInventory()` (which calls `connection()`) before rendering anything, including the title.

**What changed:** The page is now split so the static shell renders immediately and inventory streams in behind a Suspense boundary:

```1:27:app/product/page.tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'
import { getInventory } from '@/lib/data'

export const unstable_instant = true

export default function ProductPage() {
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Premium Widget</h1>
      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading inventory...</p>}>
        <Inventory />
      </Suspense>
    </main>
  )
}

async function Inventory() {
  const inventory = await getInventory()
  // ...
}
```

On navigation from home, **"Premium Widget"** appears right away in the prerendered static shell. Stock count and price load afterward inside the Suspense fallback. `unstable_instant` enables dev-time checks that this route stays instant on client navigations.

